public class CarAnalyzer {
    public static Map<String, Integer> findMostPopularCarColor(List<Car> cars) {
        // Collect the colors of all cars in a map where the key is the color and the value is the count
        Map<String, Integer> colorCounts = cars.stream()
                                                .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Car::getColor, Collectors.counting()));

        // Find the most popular color
        String mostPopularColor = colorCounts.entrySet().stream()
                                                .max(Map.Entry.comparingByValue())
                                                .map(Map.Entry::getKey)
                                                .orElse(null);

        // Return a map with the count and color of the most popular car
        return new HashMap<String, Integer>() {{
            put("count", colorCounts.get(mostPopularColor));
            put("color", mostPopularColor);
        }};
    }
}
```

This method uses Java Streams to count the occurrences of each car color and then finds the color with the highest count. It returns a map containing the count and the color of the most popular car.

